BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:finnish-cultural-foundation-october-round-2026@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Finnish Cultural Foundation: October Round 2026 (all fiel
 ds of art and science)
DESCRIPTION:Finland's largest private foundation moves to a single joint ap
 plication round in 2026: the central fund and all 17 regional funds accept
  applications together from 15 to 30 October. It funds all fields of art a
 nd science\, with one-year and multi-year working grants as the cornerston
 e alongside project grants for individuals\, working groups and organisati
 ons. SCALE: around EUR 49 million awarded annually across roughly 2\,100 g
 rants (about 20\,600 applications in 2025\, including 165 multi-year grant
 s)\; recent October rounds averaged over 450 grants of one or more years\,
  and working grants can extend up to four years. ELIGIBILITY: Finnish nati
 onals and people or organisations residing or working in Finland\; other a
 pplicants qualify if the application demonstrates clear\, strong ties to F
 inland or Finnish culture. HOW: apply online during the window via the fou
 ndation's grant service. DEADLINE: 30 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Finni
 sh Cultural Foundation (Suomen Kulttuurirahasto)\nLocation: Finland. Open 
 to Finnish nationals\, people and organisations residing or working in Fin
 land\, and other applicants with demonstrable strong ties to Finland or Fi
 nnish culture.\nAward: Around EUR 49 million awarded annually across rough
 ly 2\,100 grants\; recent October rounds have averaged over 450 working an
 d project grants covering one or more years\, with working grants extendin
 g up to four years. No application fee.\nDuration: Working grants of one t
 o four years\; project grants per project\n\nMore: https://skr.fi/en/grant
 s/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://skr.fi/en/grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Finland. Open to Finnish nationals\, people and organisations resi
 ding or working in Finland\, and other applicants with demonstrable strong
  ties to Finland or Finnish culture.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unearthodox-exploration-co-lab-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261116
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261117
SUMMARY:Deadline: Unearthodox Exploration Co-Lab 2027: Edges of Possibility
DESCRIPTION:Online incubator from Swiss foundation Unearthodox (formerly th
 e Luc Hoffmann Institute) for innovators with early-stage ideas at the int
 ersection of environmental and societal challenges\, aimed at work that ta
 ckles root causes in the relationship between people\, society and nature 
 rather than symptoms: climate\, biodiversity\, habitat loss\, regeneration
  and environmental justice among them. WHAT YOU GET: a CHF 10\,000 grant p
 lus 10 months of cohort-based incubation (March to December 2027) with coa
 ching\, expert and peer support\, and access to a global community of syst
 ems innovators. ELIGIBILITY: over 18\, idea already in motion through rese
 arch\, testing\, piloting or community engagement\; applications in Englis
 h\; participation fully online with sessions planned for UTC-6 to UTC+6. S
 ELECTION CRITERIA: systems orientation (25 percent)\, nature-society visio
 n (25 percent)\, boundary-pushing (25 percent)\, transformational intent (
 15 percent)\, edge-walking (10 percent). DEADLINE: 16 November 2026\, 23:5
 9 GMT+1 (window opened 15 September 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Unearthodox\nL
 ocation: Online\; group sessions designed around time zones UTC-6 to UTC+6
 . Open worldwide to applicants over 18\; applications in English.\nAward: 
 CHF 10\,000 grant per selected initiative\, plus a 10-month incubation pro
 gramme with tailored coaching\, expert support\, peer learning\, systems m
 apping and futures-thinking support. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 mon
 ths\, 1 March to 31 December 2027\n\nMore: https://unearthodox.org/2026/09
 /open-call-edges-of-possibility-exploration-co-lab-2027/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unearthodox.org/2026/09/open-call-edges-of-possibility-explorat
 ion-co-lab-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\; group sessions designed around time zones UTC-6 to UTC+6.
  Open worldwide to applicants over 18\; applications in English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fonds-soziokultur-allgemeine-projektfoerderung-2026-nov@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Soziokultur: General Project Funding\, November 202
 6 round (Allgemeine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Twice-yearly open round of Germany's federal fund for participa
 tory and sociocultural arts projects: community-rooted work that uses arti
 stic means (performance\, media\, music\, visual art\, digital culture) to
  engage people in social questions. Strong fit for artist collectives and 
 small cultural organisations doing participatory\, socially engaged or civ
 ic-media work in Germany. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 5\,000 to EUR 30\,000\, up to 
 80 percent of the project budget\, decided in January 2027 with project st
 arts from February 2027. ELIGIBILITY: legal entities and groups (associati
 ons\, initiatives of at least three people resident in Germany\, GbR\, Gmb
 H\, UG\, private foundations)\; individuals cannot apply alone. Organisati
 ons that received two consecutive grants must sit out two rounds. The fund
  explicitly welcomes applications from people with disabilities\, non-nati
 ve speakers and non-academics. DEADLINE: 2 November 2026 via the applicati
 on portal (window opened 2 October)\; a digital info session runs on 14 Oc
 tober 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Soziokultur\nLocation: Germany. Project
 s must take place in Germany\; applicant groups need at least three member
 s resident in Germany.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to EUR 30\,000 per project\, cov
 ering at most 80 percent of the total project budget. No application fee.\
 nDuration: Project-length\; funded projects can start from February 2027.\
 n\nMore: https://www.fonds-soziokultur.de/en/projectfunding/overview?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.fonds-soziokultur.de/en/projectfunding/overview?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany. Projects must take place in Germany\; applicant groups ne
 ed at least three members resident in Germany.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cerv-2026-citizens-rem@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270224
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270225
SUMMARY:Deadline: EU CERV: European Remembrance 2026-27 (CERV-2026-CITIZENS
 -REM)
DESCRIPTION:The EU's main remembrance funding line\, and emphatically not H
 olocaust-only: the 2026-27 call (covering both years\; there is no separat
 e 2027 call) funds projects across four topics: 1) remembering democratic 
 transitions and the (re)building of democratic institutions\; 2) remembran
 ce of the Holocaust against Jewish people\; 3) remembrance of the Holocaus
 t\, acts of genocide\, war crimes and crimes against humanity\, with prior
 ities on Roma victims and on LGBTIQ+ and other victims\; 4) the legacy of 
 colonialism\, slavery and migration in contemporary multicultural European
  societies. Previous rounds funded exhibitions\, digital archives\, testim
 ony projects\, memorial education and artistic memory work. ELIGIBILITY: l
 ead applicant must be a non-profit legal entity (public or private) or int
 ernational organisation established in an EU Member State or CERV-associat
 ed country\; for-profits only as co-applicants alongside public or non-pro
 fit partners\; each application addresses exactly one topic. TIMELINE: cal
 l opens 21 October 2026\; deadline 24 February 2027 at 17:00 CET\, via the
  EU Funding and Tenders Portal.\n\nOrganisation: European Commission / EAC
 EA (Citizens\, Equality\, Rights and Values Programme)\nLocation: EU Membe
 r States (incl. OCTs) and CERV-associated countries. Lead applicant must b
 e a non-profit legal entity or international organisation.\nAward: EUR 50\
 ,000 to EUR 500\,000 per project\, from an estimated call budget of EUR 28
  million (EUR 14M Holocaust remembrance of Jewish victims\; EUR 5M genocid
 e\, war crimes and crimes against humanity incl. Roma and LGBTIQ+ victims\
 ; EUR 5M colonialism\, slavery and migration\; EUR 4M democratic transitio
 ns). No application fee.\nDuration: Projects typically 12 to 24 months\n\n
 More: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/scree
 n/opportunities/topic-search?keywords=CERV-2026-CITIZENS-REM&utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-search?keywords=CERV-2026-CITIZENS-REM&utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States (incl. OCTs) and CERV-associated countries. Lead 
 applicant must be a non-profit legal entity or international organisation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:oasis-bom-dia-cultivamos-cultura-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: OASis Bom Dia Residency 2027 at Cultivamos Cultura (Sao L
 uis\, Portugal)
DESCRIPTION:Cultivamos Cultura in Sao Luis (Odemira\, Portugal) hosts the B
 om Dia residency as part of the European OASis project: one proposal is se
 lected for a 7-to-30-day residency during March 2027. Residents engage wit
 h the local community (artist talks\, walks\, workshops\, open studios) an
 d must produce an output for the OASis group exhibition in 2027\; one outp
 ut is added to Cultivamos Cultura's collection\, and documentation is shar
 ed across OASis partner channels. WHO: international creators\, artists an
 d researchers from various fields and disciplines\, including practitioner
 s working at the intersection of culture and other disciplines\; individua
 ls or groups of up to two people (conditions and funding are the same for 
 a pair as for one individual)\; selected residents must be physically pres
 ent for the approved timeline and reasonably autonomous in producing the p
 roject. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 1\,300 project fee\, travel budget up to EUR 500
 \, production and material expenses up to EUR 1\,600 (approved by Cultivam
 os Cultura before purchase\, paid against an invoice)\, equitable food per
  diem\, accommodation in a private room in a shared farmhouse on the Culti
 vamos Cultura property with shared kitchen\, a workspace or studio\, and f
 ree access to all spaces and resources. APPLICATION: via Google Form\; the
  call runs 18 September to 30 October 2026\, 18:00 CET\, but closes early 
 once 100 applications are received\, so apply promptly. Results announced 
 in the third week of December 2026\; no individual feedback. Full details 
 at cultivamoscultura.com.\n\nOrganisation: Cultivamos Cultura (European OA
 Sis project)\nLocation: Sao Luis\, Odemira\, Portugal. Open to internation
 al applicants.\nAward: EUR 1\,300 project fee\, travel budget up to EUR 50
 0\, production and material expenses up to EUR 1\,600 (pre-approved)\, foo
 d per diem\, plus free accommodation in a private room in a shared farmhou
 se and access to a workspace or studio and all Cultivamos Cultura spaces a
 nd resources.\nDuration: 7 to 30 days during March 2027.\n\nMore: https://
 docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf_PzJ3DgPiR8eVotOM0WqkCF2kebzzfkSjOZkvX6
 afx5xoQw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf_PzJ3DgPiR8eVotOM0WqkCF2kebz
 zfkSjOZkvX6afx5xoQw/viewform?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Sao Luis\, Odemira\, Portugal. Open to international applicants.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kooperativa-fai-mobility-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270301
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270302
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kooperativa x Flanders Arts Institute: South-Eastern Euro
 pe Mobility Programme 2026-27
DESCRIPTION:Flanders Arts Institute and the Kooperativa network offer fifte
 en mobility grants for Flanders-based artists and arts professionals in th
 e visual arts\, performing arts\, music and sound to immerse themselves in
  the South-Eastern European arts sector. Participants spend 3 to 5 days jo
 b shadowing at one organisation in Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Montenegro\, C
 roatia\, Kosovo\, North Macedonia\, Serbia or Slovenia\, with mobility act
 ions between 1 October 2026 and 30 June 2027. WHAT YOU GET: travel costs\,
  accommodation and per diems per Erasmus+ formulas\, plus up to EUR 300 fo
 r the host to cover any costs they might incur. ELIGIBILITY: artists and a
 rts professionals based in Flanders\, Belgium. APPLICATION: two steps\; fi
 rst email ward@kunsten.be with an outline of the project status\, then sub
 mit a letter of intent from the host\, visit planning\, motivation and a d
 escription of the reporting format. Applications are reviewed in monthly c
 ycles (8 September\, 8 October\, 9 November\, 8 December 2026\; 15 January
 \, 8 February\, 8 March 2027) and are accepted until 1 March 2027. AFTERWA
 RDS: participants share their experience through a written report\, video\
 , talk or recording on an online platform.\n\nOrganisation: Flanders Arts 
 Institute (Kunstenpunt) and Kooperativa\nLocation: Job shadowing at arts o
 rganisations in Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Montenegro\, Croatia\, Kosovo\, N
 orth Macedonia\, Serbia or Slovenia. Open to artists and arts professional
 s based in Flanders (Belgium) only.\nAward: Fully funded mobility: travel 
 costs\, accommodation and per diems calculated per Erasmus+ formulas\, plu
 s up to EUR 300 for the host organisation's costs. Fifteen grants availabl
 e. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 5 days of job shadowing at one orga
 nisation\, with mobility actions taking place between 1 October 2026 and 3
 0 June 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kooperativa-x-fai-mo
 bility-programme-immerse-yourself-in-the-southeastern-european-arts-sector
 /?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kunsten.be/en/calls/kooperativa-x-fai-mobility-programme-im
 merse-yourself-in-the-southeastern-european-arts-sector/?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Job shadowing at arts organisations in Bosnia and Herzegovina\, Mo
 ntenegro\, Croatia\, Kosovo\, North Macedonia\, Serbia or Slovenia. Open t
 o artists and arts professionals based in Flanders (Belgium) only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lendhauer-urban-ecologies-klagenfurt-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: Lendhauer: Urban Ecologies - Coexistence and Control (Len
 dhafen\, Klagenfurt 2027)
DESCRIPTION:The Klagenfurt association Lendhauer invites proposals for artw
 orks at the Lendhafen\, the city's harbour\, under the 2027 theme Urban Ec
 ologies: Coexistence and Control. The call asks who or what counts as usef
 ul or disruptive in public space\, who is included or excluded\, and wheth
 er peaceful coexistence is achievable\, treating urban space as networks o
 f diverse relationships between human and non-human actors. Both fully dev
 eloped artistic works and experimental\, process-based or collaborative ap
 proaches are welcome. WHAT YOU GET: production costs up to EUR 4\,000 gros
 s (exact amount depends on project scope)\, an artist fee up to EUR 2\,500
  gross\, travel expenses up to EUR 1\,000\, and on-site coordination of te
 chnical and organisational requirements including permits. ELIGIBILITY: ar
 tists\, designers\, architects\, performers\, theorists and practitioners 
 working in interdisciplinary contexts\; individuals and collectives\, base
 d in Austria or abroad\; disciplines listed are architecture\, performing 
 arts\, and visual arts and design. Projects are realised June to end of Se
 ptember 2027. DEADLINE: 2 November 2026. Full details and application via 
 lendhafen.at.\n\nOrganisation: Lendhauer (Klagenfurt\, Austria)\nLocation:
  Lendhafen harbour\, Klagenfurt\, Austria. Open to individuals and collect
 ives based in Austria or abroad.\nAward: Artist fee up to EUR 2\,500 gross
 \, production costs up to EUR 4\,000 gross (depending on project scope)\, 
 and travel expenses up to EUR 1\,000. No application fee.\nDuration: Proje
 cts realised at the Lendhafen between June and the end of September 2027.\
 n\nMore: https://www.lendhafen.at/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.lendhafen.at/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Lendhafen harbour\, Klagenfurt\, Austria. Open to individuals and 
 collectives based in Austria or abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-embassy-brussels-cultural-support-nov-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Embassy in Brussels: Open Call for Cultural P
 roject Support
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Embassy in Brussels runs several open calls per
  year subsidising Dutch-Belgian artistic and cultural projects in Belgium 
 that strengthen the Netherlands' cultural profile and promote cooperation 
 between the two countries. All artistic disciplines are eligible\, with a 
 focus on performing arts\, visual arts\, cultural heritage\, creative indu
 stries and digital culture\; the embassy welcomes innovative formats\, cro
 ss-border exchange\, and work on participation\, inclusion\, equal rights 
 and sustainability. The subsidy (max EUR 5\,000) only covers costs related
  to the Dutch participation in the project\, such as travel and accommodat
 ion for Dutch participants\, art transport\, production\, and communicatio
 n for the Dutch segment. Projects must take place in Belgium (unless virtu
 al collaborations) and be accessible to the public\; personal development 
 projects are not eligible. ELIGIBILITY: professional creators\, organisati
 ons\, institutions and legal entities in Belgium with a company registrati
 on number\; Dutch artists typically take part via a Belgian partner or org
 aniser. Apply via the embassy (netherlandsandyou.nl). DEADLINES: 3 Novembe
 r 2026\, then 18 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of the Kingdom of th
 e Netherlands in Brussels\nLocation: Belgium. Applicants must be professio
 nal creators\, organisations\, institutions or legal entities in Belgium w
 ith a company registration number\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of D
 utch-Belgian projects.\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 per project.\nDuration: Ro
 lling open calls with multiple deadlines per year\; next deadlines 3 Novem
 ber 2026 and 18 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlem
 bassy-brussels-open-call-for-support?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlembassy-brussels-open-call-for-suppo
 rt?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgium. Applicants must be professional creators\, organisations\
 , institutions or legal entities in Belgium with a company registration nu
 mber\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dutch-Belgian projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027: Energy G
 hosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:The Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Program is an annual fellow
 ship offering four fully funded fellowships to artists from around the wor
 ld\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with V
 ISIT\, the artist-in-residence programme of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK L
 uckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art (Warsaw). The
  2027 edition particularly encourages projects at the intersection of art\
 , energy and ecology exploring the theme ENERGY GHOSTS: the unseen dimensi
 ons of energy approached through mythology\, cosmology or speculative fict
 ion\, the invisible infrastructures\, histories and residues that haunt co
 ntemporary life\, and energy as an ecological\, political or spiritual for
 ce. Proposals are welcome from visual art\, performance\, film\, installat
 ion\, sound\, writing and new media. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 20\,000 per fellow 
 for artist fees and production costs of a new project (research and develo
 pment\, travel\, material and presentation costs)\; three fellows receive 
 studio space and accommodation at E-WERK Luckenwalde (a former power stati
 on about 40 minutes south of Berlin)\, one is accommodated by the Akademie
  der Künste in Berlin. The three-month residency runs roughly September t
 o November 2027 with on-site presence of at least 75% required\, a retreat
  at Ujazdowski Castle in Warsaw in September 2027\, events across the thre
 e venues\, and a closing symposium in October 2027 at the Akademie der Kü
 nste where fellows show work in progress alongside the 2026 cohort. JURY: 
 Nolan Oswald Dennis\; Chus Martinez (Institute Art Gender Nature\, TBA21)\
 ; Sarah Johanna Theurer (Fondation Beyeler)\; Anh-Linh Ngo (Akademie der K
 ünste)\; and Tiara Roxanne. APPLICATION: via the VISIT portal at visit-en
 ergy.com/bewerben. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation:
  JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Akademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-
 WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocati
 on: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie de
 r Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in
  Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fel
 lowships of EUR 20\,000 each\, intended for artist fees and production cos
 ts of a new project (research and development\, travel\, materials and pre
 sentation costs)\, plus studio space and accommodation for the three-month
  residency.\nDuration: Three months\, roughly September to November 2027 (
 the AdK notice gives mid-August to mid-November)\; fellows must live and w
 ork on site at least 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10
 /open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:art4mental-open-call-vr-artists-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
SUMMARY:Deadline: ART4MENTAL open call for artists: VR content for mental-h
 ealth support (EUR 5\,000 sub-grants)
DESCRIPTION:ART4MENTAL is a Creative Europe project (partners in Ukraine\, 
 Poland\, Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria) selecting 20 artists to c
 reate immersive VR content and scenarios used in art-therapy and mental-he
 alth support sessions across Ukraine and the EU. Selected artists get prof
 essional training in VR technology and trauma-informed design\, local boot
 camps\, a residency in Ukraine's Carpathian Mountains\, study visits to re
 habilitation centres\, ongoing collaboration with mental-health profession
 als\, and present their work at European exhibitions and conferences\, inc
 luding an international exhibition in Poland. ELIGIBILITY: the official pa
 ge says residents of EU countries and Ukraine with a proven artistic pract
 ice and full availability for all mandatory activities\; the On the Move l
 isting adds that at least 10 of the 20 places go to artists from Ukraine a
 nd at least one each to Czechia\, Estonia\, Sweden and Austria\, so applic
 ants from other EU countries are eligible but not prioritised. Two stages:
  online form with supporting documents\, then an online interview\; select
 ed artists announced January 2027. DEADLINE: 11 November 2026 per On the M
 ove (the official page only says November 2026\; no time zone stated).\n\n
 Organisation: ART4MENTAL (Creative Europe project)\nLocation: Hybrid: onli
 ne training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountains\, Ukraine\, and a
 n exhibition in Poland.\nAward: Sub-grant of up to EUR 5\,000 per artist f
 or 20 selected artists (EUR 100\,000 pool)\, plus VR training\, mentorship
 \, a residency in the Ukrainian Carpathians and exhibition opportunities. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: Selection by January 2027\; residency and e
 xhibition dates not yet published.\n\nMore: https://www.art4mental.com/app
 lication?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.art4mental.com/application?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hybrid: online training plus a residency in the Carpathian Mountai
 ns\, Ukraine\, and an exhibition in Poland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:braid-creative-commissions-a-promise-in-return-2027@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: BRAID Creative Commissions 2027: A Promise in Return (Res
 ponsible AI\, GBP 8\,000-12\,000\, Edinburgh Art Festival)
DESCRIPTION:BRAID\, the UKRI AHRC-funded Responsible AI programme at the Un
 iversity of Edinburgh\, is commissioning around seven creative works that 
 treat Responsible AI as a question of relationships\, commitments and obli
 gations rather than a technical checklist or a set of rules\, under the ti
 tle A Promise in Return. WHO: UK-based creative practitioners in any mediu
 m: artists\, designers\, musicians and performers\, architects and urban d
 esigners\, craftspeople and artisans\, writers and poets. Full-time underg
 raduate and taught postgraduate students are not eligible\; PhD students m
 ay apply if registered as self-employed freelancers. WHAT YOU GET: a commi
 ssion budget of GBP 8\,000 to 12\,000\, production support from Inspace an
 d the Institute for Design Informatics\, and presentation during the Edinb
 urgh Art Festival in August 2027 with the Edinburgh Futures Institute. APP
 LICATION: online form (written or an eight-minute video application) plus 
 a single PDF of portfolio\, CV and budget emailed to braid@ed.ac.uk\; late
  submissions are not accepted. DEADLINE: Monday 2 November 2026 at 17:00 G
 MT.\n\nOrganisation: BRAID (Bridging Responsible AI Divides)\, University 
 of Edinburgh\, with Inspace\, the Institute for Design Informatics and the
  Edinburgh Futures Institute\nLocation: UK. For UK-based creative practiti
 oners\; work is presented in Edinburgh during the Edinburgh Art Festival\,
  August 2027.\nAward: Around seven commissions with budgets of GBP 8\,000 
 to 12\,000 each\, inclusive of VAT and all costs. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Projects run January to August 2027\, presented during the Edinburg
 h Art Festival in August 2027\, with possible further displays through 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://braiduk.org/creative-commissions?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:UK. For UK-based creative practitioners\; work is presented in Edi
 nburgh during the Edinburgh Art Festival\, August 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture-helps-solidarity-collaboration-grants-2026-round-2@artificialno
 uveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Helps Solidarity Collaboration Grants\, final cal
 l (Ukrainian-led cross-border partnerships\, up to EUR 20\,000-30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:The second and final round of Culture Helps Solidarity Collabor
 ation Grants\, run by the European Cultural Foundation through its Culture
  of Solidarity Fund with Insha Osvita\, VETERANKA Movement and zusa\, and 
 funded by Creative Europe. It supports cultural projects that improve acce
 ss to culture and promote inclusion and mental well-being for internally d
 isplaced people and refugees from Ukraine\, helping integrate them into ho
 st communities through intercultural dialogue\, professional exchange and 
 long-term solidarity\; vulnerable groups and veterans are an emphasis. WHO
 : partnerships of at least two organisations\, with at least one Ukrainian
 -led organisation (in Ukraine or in exile) and at least one based in a Cre
 ative Europe country\; cross-border partnerships and Ukrainian-led partner
 ships with neighbouring Creative Europe countries are prioritised. A match
 making board helps applicants find partners. WHAT YOU GET: up to EUR 20\,0
 00 for two-partner projects or up to EUR 30\,000 for three or more partner
 s\; at least 15 projects will be awarded. APPLICATION: read the Call for P
 roposals PDF on the call page and apply via the Culture of Solidarity Fund
  grant platform. DEADLINE: 10 November 2026\, 13:00 Amsterdam time (14:00 
 Kyiv).\n\nOrganisation: European Cultural Foundation with Insha Osvita\, V
 ETERANKA Movement and zusa (Creative Europe project)\nLocation: Partnershi
 ps of at least two organisations: at least one Ukrainian-led (based in Ukr
 aine or operating in exile) and at least one based in a Creative Europe co
 untry.\nAward: Up to EUR 20\,000 for a partnership of two organisations\, 
 up to EUR 30\,000 for three or more\; at least 15 projects funded. No appl
 ication fee mentioned.\nDuration: Per project\; Culture Helps Solidarity r
 uns October 2025 to March 2028.\n\nMore: https://culturehelpssolidarity.eu
 /collaboration-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://culturehelpssolidarity.eu/collaboration-grants/?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Partnerships of at least two organisations: at least one Ukrainian
 -led (based in Ukraine or operating in exile) and at least one based in a 
 Creative Europe country.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hordaland-kunstsenter-nordic-baltic-residency-2027-2028@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Hordaland Kunstsenter Nordic and Baltic Residency 2027/20
 28 (Bergen\, NOK 30\,000 stipend)
DESCRIPTION:Hordaland Kunstsenter\, founded in 1976 as Norway's first artis
 t-run art centre\, invites artists based in the Nordic and Baltic countrie
 s to apply for its 2027/2028 residency programme in central Bergen\, suppo
 rted by the Nordic-Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture. The centre does 
 not privilege any medium and is especially interested in practices that mo
 ve between disciplines\, including exhibition-making\, performance\, sound
 \, publishing\, moving image\, socially engaged and research-based or disc
 ursive work. WHO: artists with a permanent address in Sapmi\, Denmark\, Fi
 nland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Iceland\, Sweden\, Aland\, Estonia
 \, Latvia or Lithuania (citizenship not required)\; artists based in Norwa
 y\, full-time students and artistic PhD candidates are not eligible\; visa
  costs are the resident's own. WHAT YOU GET: a NOK 30\,000 stipend for the
  full-time two-month residency\, a furnished one-bedroom self-catering apa
 rtment near the centre\, up to EUR 500 travel support booked by the reside
 ncy coordinator\, a dedicated desk and workspace\, access to the project r
 oom\, and connections to studios\, specialist workspaces and production ne
 tworks in Bergen. Residents give a public presentation or talk during thei
 r stay. APPLICATION: fill in the Google form on the call page and email on
 e PDF (CV\, motivation letter on intentions and use of time\, up to 5 slid
 es of recent work) to residency@kunstsenter.no\; questions to scott@kunsts
 enter.no. DEADLINE: 1 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Hordaland Kunstsente
 r\nLocation: Bergen\, Norway. For artists with a permanent address in the 
 Nordic region (Sapmi\, Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\,
  Iceland\, Sweden\, Aland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia\, Latvia\, Lit
 huania)\; citizenship not required. Not open to artists based in Norway.\n
 Award: NOK 30\,000 stipend for the two-month residency\, accommodation cov
 ered\, up to EUR 500 travel support\, and a dedicated desk and workspace. 
 No application fee.\nDuration: 2 months\, in one of four periods: spring 2
 027\, fall 2027\, winter 2027 or spring 2028.\n\nMore: https://kunstsenter
 .no/triangle/5?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kunstsenter.no/triangle/5?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Bergen\, Norway. For artists with a permanent address in the Nordi
 c region (Sapmi\, Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland\, Icel
 and\, Sweden\, Aland) or the Baltic countries (Estonia\, Latvia\, Lithuani
 a)\; citizenship not required. Not open to artists based in Norway.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-europe-media-literacy-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Europe Media Literacy 2027 (up to EUR 500\,000 p
 er project)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Europe's Media Literacy call (CREA-CROSS-2027-MEDIALIT
 ERACY) funds cross-border actions that build media literacy and resilience
  to disinformation\, with attention to countries facing particular media l
 iteracy challenges. WHO: consortia of at least three entities from three e
 ligible Creative Europe countries\; individuals cannot apply. WHAT YOU GET
 : up to EUR 500\,000 per project at a 70 percent funding rate\, from a tot
 al budget of EUR 3\,500\,000. APPLICATION: via the EU Funding and Tenders 
 portal. DEADLINE: 20 January 2027\, 17:00 CET (Brussels).\n\nOrganisation:
  Creative Europe Cross-sectoral strand (European Commission / EACEA)\nLoca
 tion: EU Member States and countries associated to Creative Europe. For or
 ganisations (legal entities) established in an eligible country\; natural 
 persons cannot apply.\nAward: Up to EUR 500\,000 per project at a 70 perce
 nt funding rate\; total call budget EUR 3\,500\,000. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Projects normally up to 24 months. Call opened 22 October 2026.\
 n\nMore: https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/sc
 reen/opportunities/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-MEDIALITERACY?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-MEDIALITERACY?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States and countries associated to Creative Europe. For 
 organisations (legal entities) established in an eligible country\; natura
 l persons cannot apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-europe-journalism-partnerships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270205
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Europe Journalism Partnerships 2027: Collaborati
 ons and Pluralism (up to EUR 2-2.5 million per project)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Europe's Journalism Partnerships call (CREA-CROSS-2027
 -JOURPART) has two topics supporting the news media sector. COLLABORATIONS
  funds cross-border collaboration and business transformation among news m
 edia organisations\; consortia need at least three independent entities fr
 om three eligible countries. PLURALISM supports journalism sectors of publ
 ic interest (for example local and regional media\, investigative or commu
 nity journalism)\, with at least 60 percent of the grant going to that sec
 tor\, including through re-granting of up to EUR 60\,000 per third party\;
  applicants can be single organisations or consortia\, with activities in 
 at least four EU Member States. WHAT YOU GET: up to EUR 2\,000\,000 per Co
 llaborations project (80 percent funding) or up to EUR 2\,500\,000 per Plu
 ralism project (90 percent funding)\, from EUR 7\,000\,000 per topic. Indi
 viduals cannot apply. APPLICATION: via the EU Funding and Tenders portal (
 topics CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART-COLLABORATIONS and -PLURALISM). DEADLINE: 
 4 February 2027\, 17:00 CET (Brussels).\n\nOrganisation: Creative Europe C
 ross-sectoral strand (European Commission / EACEA)\nLocation: EU Member St
 ates and countries associated to Creative Europe. For organisations (legal
  entities) established in an eligible country\; natural persons cannot app
 ly.\nAward: Total EUR 14\,000\,000 (EUR 7\,000\,000 per topic). Collaborat
 ions: up to EUR 2\,000\,000 per project at 80 percent funding. Pluralism: 
 up to EUR 2\,500\,000 per project at 90 percent funding\, with re-granting
  of up to EUR 60\,000 per third party. No application fee.\nDuration: Proj
 ects normally up to 24 months. Call opened 22 October 2026.\n\nMore: https
 ://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportuni
 ties/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART-PLURALISM?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-details/CREA-CROSS-2027-JOURPART-PLURALISM?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States and countries associated to Creative Europe. For 
 organisations (legal entities) established in an eligible country\; natura
 l persons cannot apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:culture-moves-europe-residency-hosts-2026-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270119
SUMMARY:Deadline: Culture Moves Europe: Call for Residency Hosts 2026-2027 
 (EUR 50/day per resident for hosting organisations)
DESCRIPTION:The organisation-side strand of Culture Moves Europe\, the EU's
  flagship mobility scheme for artists and cultural professionals\, funds o
 rganisations to host artists in residence. WHO: newly or well-established 
 legal entities registered and based in a Creative Europe country and activ
 e in architecture\, cultural heritage\, design and fashion design\, litera
 ture\, music\, performing arts or visual arts\, with capacity to host one 
 to five residents from other Creative Europe countries. WHAT YOU GET: EUR 
 50 per day per resident for the host\, plus accessibility support of EUR 3
 75\, 675 or 1\,200\; residents receive EUR 30 per day\, a travel allowance
  of EUR 400 or EUR 800 and optional top-ups (green travel\, overseas regio
 ns\, family\, visa). PROCESS: apply in English via the Goethe Application 
 Portal\, registering as Organisation/Enterprise and selecting the 2026-202
 7 call for residency hosts\; results by 9 March 2027\, then hosts select r
 esidents and submit residency info cards between 9 March and 31 July 2027\
 , with residencies starting from 12 April 2027. The call opened 15 October
  2026. DEADLINE: 18 January 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Culture Moves Europe (C
 reative Europe\, European Commission)\, implemented by the Goethe-Institut
 \nLocation: Legal entities registered in a Creative Europe country (includ
 ing overseas countries and territories and outermost regions)\, hosting 1 
 to 5 residents from other Creative Europe countries.\nAward: Hosts: EUR 50
  per day per resident plus accessibility support of EUR 375\, 675 or 1\,20
 0 depending on residency length. Residents: EUR 30 per day\, travel allowa
 nce of EUR 400 (under 5\,000 km) or EUR 800\, and top-ups for green travel
  (EUR 400)\, OCT/outermost regions (EUR 175)\, family (EUR 200 per child) 
 and visa (EUR 120). No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies from 12 Apr
 il 2027 onward\; hosts choose residents and submit residency info between 
 9 March and 31 July 2027.\n\nMore: https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-mo
 ves-europe/call-for-residency-hosts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culture.ec.europa.eu/culture-moves-europe/call-for-residency-ho
 sts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Legal entities registered in a Creative Europe country (including 
 overseas countries and territories and outermost regions)\, hosting 1 to 5
  residents from other Creative Europe countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:follow-fluxus-after-fluxus-scholarship-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Follow Fluxus: After Fluxus Scholarship 2026/27 (EUR 10\,
 000\, 3-month studio and exhibition\, Wiesbaden)
DESCRIPTION:The Follow Fluxus scholarship\, awarded by the Nassauischer Kun
 stverein Wiesbaden and the City of Wiesbaden in memory of the Fluxus movem
 ent that began in Wiesbaden in 1962\, supports artists whose work continue
 s the open\, intermedia and experimental spirit of Fluxus. WHO: internatio
 nal and national artists with a completed art degree and relevant professi
 onal and exhibition experience\; self-taught artists with notable achievem
 ents documented through exhibitions and awards may also apply. WHAT YOU GE
 T: EUR 10\,000\, a rent-free furnished live/work space with studio at the 
 Kunsthaus Wiesbaden (70.88 sqm) from 1 June to 31 August 2027\, during whi
 ch the fellow is expected to spend most of their time in Wiesbaden\, and a
 n exhibition at the Nassauischer Kunstverein afterwards. APPLICATION: uplo
 ad three PDFs (max 10 MB\; German or English) to nowtransfer.de: APF_Appli
 cantName.pdf (application letter\, CV and project outline\, one A4 page ea
 ch)\, Portfolio_ApplicantName.pdf (work examples\, exhibitions\, video/aud
 io links) and Degree_ApplicantName.pdf\; then email the download link to f
 luxus@kunstverein-wiesbaden.de with the subject 'Follow Fluxus Scholarship
  2026_27'. Postal applications are also accepted. Results by December 2026
 . DEADLINE: 1 November 2026\, email received by 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation
 : Nassauischer Kunstverein Wiesbaden\, with the City of Wiesbaden\nLocatio
 n: Wiesbaden\, Germany. Open to international and national artists.\nAward
 : EUR 10\,000 grant plus a rent-free 70.88 sqm live/work studio at the Kun
 sthaus Wiesbaden for three months and a follow-up exhibition at the Nassau
 ischer Kunstverein. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 3 months\, 1 
 June to 31 August 2027\, followed by an exhibition.\n\nMore: https://www.k
 unstverein-wiesbaden.de/en/follow-fluxus/the-scholarship/the-selection-1?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kunstverein-wiesbaden.de/en/follow-fluxus/the-scholarship/t
 he-selection-1?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Wiesbaden\, Germany. Open to international and national artists.
END:VEVENT
