SUMMARY:Deadline: HIAP x Sumud: Residency for Palestinian Artists in Helsin
 ki\, Spring 2027 (EUR 3\,600 working grant)
DESCRIPTION:HIAP and Sumud\, the Finnish Palestine Network\, invite a Pales
 tinian artist to a spring 2027 residency at the Cable Factory in Helsinki\
 , delivered through HIAP's Ukraine Solidarity Residency Programme and supp
 orted by the Finnish Ministry of Education and Culture. WHO: professional 
 contemporary artists currently based in Palestine or of Palestinian descen
 t living in the diaspora\; formal education\, exhibition history or instit
 utional recognition is not required. Family members are welcome\; collecti
 ves receive no extra grant or travel budget. WHAT YOU GET: a EUR 3\,600 wo
 rking grant\, a free 63 sqm live/work studio with kitchenette\, sleeping l
 oft and private bathroom (suited to two adults or a small family)\, one tr
 ip to and from home\, and a visa budget for application fees and travel to
  a visa office or embassy (HIAP cannot guarantee visas). APPLICATION: onli
 ne form only\, in English\; emailed applications are not considered. DEADL
 INE: 2 November 2026\, 15:00 (GMT+2).\n\nOrganisation: HIAP Helsinki Inter
 national Artist Programme\, with Sumud - The Finnish Palestine Network\nLo
 cation: Cable Factory\, Helsinki\, Finland. For professional contemporary 
 artists based in Palestine or of Palestinian descent\, including the diasp
 ora.\nAward: EUR 3\,600 working grant\, a free 63 sqm live/work studio\, o
 ne return trip\, and a visa budget covering application fees and visa-offi
 ce travel. No application fee.\nDuration: About 3 months\, 12 April to 11 
 July 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.hiap.fi/open-call/open-call-for-palestinia
 n-artists-in-helsinki-finland-spring-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.hiap.fi/open-call/open-call-for-palestinian-artists-in-hels
 inki-finland-spring-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
LOCATION:Cable Factory\, Helsinki\, Finland. For professional contemporary 
 artists based in Palestine or of Palestinian descent\, including the diasp
 ora.
