BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:daiwa-foundation-small-grants-march-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
SUMMARY:Deadline: Daiwa Foundation Small Grants\, March 2027 round (GBP 2\,
 000-9\,000 for UK-Japan projects)
DESCRIPTION:The Daiwa Foundation Small Grants support projects that promote
  interaction between the UK and Japan in any field\, including arts exchan
 ges\, exhibitions\, conferences\, grassroots and educational exchanges and
  research travel\, with travel between the two countries as the main focus
 . New initiatives are encouraged\, and gender equality and SDG themes are 
 welcome\; continuing or regular events (such as an annual festival edition
 ) are unlikely to be funded without a strong reason or special occasion. N
 OT ELIGIBLE: commissions of artworks\, capital costs\, consumables\, salar
 ies or professional fees\, tuition and commercial activity. WHAT YOU GET: 
 GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (most awards GBP 3\,000-4\,000)\, with flights funded
  up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsistence up to GBP 100 per person per day\, 
 plus GBP 50 extra per flight for environmental projects in Japan. APPLICAT
 ION: read the Application Notes\, then apply via the Foundation's online p
 ortal (separate forms for UK- and Japan-based applicants)\; advice from gr
 ants@dajf.org.uk. Decisions by late May or early June 2027. DEADLINE: 31 M
 arch 2027 (the following round closes 30 September).\n\nOrganisation: Daiw
 a Anglo-Japanese Foundation\nLocation: For individuals\, societies\, assoc
 iations and other bodies in the UK or Japan running projects that connect 
 the two countries.\nAward: GBP 2\,000 to 9\,000 (typical awards GBP 3\,000
 -4\,000)\; flights up to GBP 1\,200 each and subsistence up to GBP 100 per
  person per day. A contribution\, not full funding. No application fee.\nD
 uration: Per project\; activity can start from late May or early June 2027
 .\n\nMore: https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-s
 mall-grants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://dajf.org.uk/grants-awards-and-prizes/daiwa-foundation-small-gra
 nts?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For individuals\, societies\, associations and other bodies in the
  UK or Japan running projects that connect the two countries.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:istka-2026-creative-economy-programme@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261030T153558Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261204
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261205
SUMMARY:Deadline: Istanbul Development Agency (ISTKA): 2026 Creative Econom
 y Strengthening Financial Support Programme
DESCRIPTION:ISTKA's 2026 Creative Economy programme (ISTKA/2026/YEG) funds 
 projects that strengthen Istanbul's cultural and creative economy. Priorit
 y 1 covers innovative\, scalable infrastructure\, platforms and business m
 odels for cultural and creative actors\, with example topics including new
  media\, digital art\, AI and blockchain tools\, 3D scanning and digital a
 rchives. Priority 2 covers the city's creative identity\, for example arti
 stic and design interventions in public space and residency models. ELIGIB
 ILITY: Istanbul-based public bodies and municipalities\, chambers and prof
 essional bodies\, non-profit cooperatives\, NGOs (associations\, foundatio
 ns\, federations)\, universities\, institutes and research infrastructures
 \, technopark management companies and technology transfer offices\; indiv
 iduals and for-profit companies cannot lead. APPLICATION: via the KAYS sys
 tem with application form\, budget\, logical framework\, key-staff CVs and
  standard contract annexes\; questions to yes@istka.org.tr no later than 2
 0 days before the deadline. DEADLINE: 4 December 2026\, 23:59 in KAYS\; si
 gned commitment letter due 11 December 2026\, 17:00.\n\nOrganisation: Ista
 nbul Development Agency (ISTKA)\nLocation: Istanbul\, Turkiye. Lead applic
 ants must be legal entities registered or headquartered in Istanbul.\nAwar
 d: TRY 300\,000\,000 programme total. TRY 5\,000\,000 minimum and TRY 20\,
 000\,000 maximum per project\, covering 25 to 75 percent of eligible costs
  (co-financing required). No application fee.\nDuration: 12 to 18 months\n
 \nMore: https://www.istka.org.tr/duyuru/2026-yili-yaratici-ekonominin-gucl
 endirilmesi-mali-destek-programi-1zsq?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.istka.org.tr/duyuru/2026-yili-yaratici-ekonominin-guclendir
 ilmesi-mali-destek-programi-1zsq?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
LOCATION:Istanbul\, Turkiye. Lead applicants must be legal entities registe
 red or headquartered in Istanbul.
END:VEVENT
